WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:10.500
Hello everyone

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.133
welcome to the Market Opening Bell for Thursday

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:14.000
May 7

00:00:14.333 --> 00:00:16.633
your 10-minute guide to the stock market

00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:21.766
Market sentiment is optimistic about a potential US-Iran agreement

00:00:21.933 --> 00:00:23.233
US stock futures rose

00:00:23.233 --> 00:00:26.000
driving Hong Kong stocks higher in early trading

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.033
The Hang Seng Index opened up 131 points

00:00:29.033 --> 00:00:37.266
then extended gains to close at the day’s high of 26213, up 315 points or 1.2%.

00:00:37.666 --> 00:00:43.266
The H-share Index rose 70 points or 0.8% to close at 8800

00:00:43.966 --> 00:00:51.400
The Hang Seng Tech Index gained 39 points or 0.8% to close at 4969

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:55.500
Total market turnover reached HK$304.7 billion

00:00:56.033 --> 00:01:02.266
Southbound Stock Connect funds recorded a net outflow of HK$8.565 billion

00:01:02.866 --> 00:01:04.366
Key flows included:

00:01:04.366 --> 00:01:05.166
•  Net buying:

00:01:05.166 --> 00:01:09.400
Cambridge Technology +HK$144 million

00:01:09.966 --> 00:01:10.966
•  Net selling:

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.033
Tracker Fund -HK$3.739 billion

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:16.600
Tencent -HK$2.397 billion

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.300
Xiaomi -HK$1.049 billion

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:23.966
Hang Seng China Enterprises Index ETF -HK$741 million

00:01:23.966 --> 00:01:26.200
Pop Mart -HK$388 million

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:30.566
Yangtze Optical Fibre and Cable -HK$266 million

00:01:30.566 --> 00:01:33.533
Hua Hong Semiconductor -HK$168 million

00:01:33.533 --> 00:01:35.166
According to statistics

00:01:35.166 --> 00:01:39.633
Southbound funds have net bought CNOOC for 16 consecutive days

00:01:39.633 --> 00:01:42.333
totaling HK$7.022 billion;

00:01:43.066 --> 00:01:46.600
net sold Alibaba for 9 consecutive days

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:49.266
totaling HK$4.862 billion;

00:01:49.266 --> 00:01:52.333
and net sold Tencent for 6 consecutive days

00:01:52.333 --> 00:01:55.333
totaling HK$6.117 billion

00:01:55.333 --> 00:01:56.000
Technically

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.933
the Hang Seng Index has reclaimed the 26000-point level

00:01:59.933 --> 00:02:04.733
Although it reached an intraday high of 26213 points

00:02:04.733 --> 00:02:09.300
it has not yet broken through the May 4 high of 26

00:02:09.433 --> 00:02:11.466
326 points

00:02:11.466 --> 00:02:12.133
Nevertheless

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:15.766
the closing index set a new high since April 21

00:02:15.933 --> 00:02:21.766
when the Hang Seng Index hit its peak of 26529 points

00:02:21.766 --> 00:02:26.900
With the US-Iran situation easing and strong performance in overseas markets

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:33.166
the Hang Seng Index is expected to challenge the 26529-point level

00:02:33.233 --> 00:02:36.766
If it successfully breaks above this high

00:02:36.766 --> 00:02:39.400
the next target would be 26700 points

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.266
On the first trading day after the May 1 holiday

00:02:44.266 --> 00:02:49.200
all three major A-share indices opened higher and continued rising

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.766
with the ChiNext board performing strongly (once up over 3%).

00:02:54.533 --> 00:02:58.466
Shanghai and Shenzhen turnover surged to over RMB 3.2 trillion

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.166
The Shanghai Composite closed at 4160

00:03:02.266 --> 00:03:04.733
up 48 points or 1.2%.

00:03:05.233 --> 00:03:10.533
The Shenzhen Component Index closed at 15459

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:13.500
up 352 points or 2.3%.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.133
The ChiNext Index closed at 3778

00:03:18.133 --> 00:03:21.000
up 101 points or 2.8%.

00:03:21.666 --> 00:03:28.400
The RMB central parity rate against the US dollar was set at 6.8562

00:03:28.433 --> 00:03:33.766
up 66 pips from the previous day — the highest since March 24

00:03:33.766 --> 00:03:34.900
2023

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:39.366
RatingDog’s April China PMI showed strong performance

00:03:39.366 --> 00:03:47.666
contrasting with the weaker official PMI and highlighting robust expansion momentum in the private economy

00:03:47.833 --> 00:03:51.066
Manufacturing PMI came in at 52.2

00:03:51.066 --> 00:04:00.300
beating market expectations of 51.0 and the prior reading of 50.8 — the fastest expansion since December 2020

00:04:00.733 --> 00:04:04.400
Production and new orders indices improved markedly

00:04:04.433 --> 00:04:12.866
Despite rising raw material costs (especially crude oil) and logistics delays caused by Middle East conflicts

00:04:12.866 --> 00:04:15.700
corporate confidence remained high

00:04:15.966 --> 00:04:26.333
Services PMI rose to 52.6 from 52.1 in March and has stayed in expansion territory for 40 consecutive months

00:04:26.333 --> 00:04:31.233
Although new export orders dipped slightly due to softer global demand

00:04:31.233 --> 00:04:34.400
domestic demand remained the main growth driver

00:04:34.466 --> 00:04:41.433
The Composite PMI Output Index climbed to 53.1 from 51.5 in March

00:04:41.433 --> 00:04:46.666
indicating a solid start for China’s private sector output in Q2

00:04:46.866 --> 00:05:07.000
Media reports citing two US officials and sources familiar with the matter say the White House believes it is close to reaching a one-page memorandum of understanding with Iran to end the war and establish a framework for more detailed subsequent nuclear negotiations

00:05:07.033 --> 00:05:09.800
The 14-point memorandum

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:11.933
reportedly just one page long

00:05:11.933 --> 00:05:20.000
would announce the end of the war in the region and initiate 30 days of negotiations for a detailed agreement

00:05:20.033 --> 00:05:24.100
possibly held in Islamabad or Geneva

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:32.433
Iran’s restrictions on shipping through the strait and the US naval blockade would be gradually lifted within those 30 days

00:05:32.433 --> 00:05:34.466
On Iran’s nuclear development

00:05:34.466 --> 00:05:43.066
the memo states that Iran will suspend uranium enrichment activities for at least 12 years

00:05:43.066 --> 00:05:46.366
though the exact duration remains negotiable

00:05:46.566 --> 00:05:47.300
On the news

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:50.300
international oil prices fell more than 10%.

00:05:50.733 --> 00:05:53.766
WTI crude broke below US$92

00:05:54.033 --> 00:05:59.400
and Brent lost the US$100 mark for the first time since April 27

00:05:59.733 --> 00:06:04.266
Spot gold broke above US$4700 per ounce

00:06:04.266 --> 00:06:07.866
Hong Kong gold-concept stocks rallied across the board

00:06:07.933 --> 00:06:11.400
Chow Tai Fook (01929) issued a profit warning (upward revision),

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:19.566
expecting net profit for the year ended March this year to rise 45–55% year-on-year

00:06:19.633 --> 00:06:21.066
The main reasons:

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:28.866
higher gold prices significantly boosted the value and gross margin of gold jewelry inventory;

00:06:28.866 --> 00:06:32.800
a more favorable sales mix in retail and high-margin jewelry (inlaid

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:32.900
jade

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.733
and “heritage” series);

00:06:34.733 --> 00:06:38.533
and strong operating leverage from strict cost control

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:43.700
Same-store sales in Hong Kong and Macau surged about 40% in Q4

00:06:43.766 --> 00:06:49.966
driven by tourism recovery and favorable tax policies boosting foot traffic

00:06:50.033 --> 00:06:51.200
In mainland China

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:54.133
despite macro headwinds affecting demand

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:58.266
directly operated stores showed resilience

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:03.666
The group is actively rolling out “new-image stores” and brand transformation

00:07:03.833 --> 00:07:12.833
Average monthly sales of new stores (around RMB 1.4 million) are significantly higher than old or closed stores

00:07:12.833 --> 00:07:15.600
improving retail efficiency

00:07:15.866 --> 00:07:18.333
Overseas semiconductor stocks surged

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:21.100
Cambricon (688256

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:23.333
SH) jumped 7.4%.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:27.166
Hong Kong-listed peers also rose sharply:

00:07:27.200 --> 00:07:29.833
SMIC (00981) +5.7%,

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:32.266
Hua Hong (01347) +9.3%.

00:07:32.433 --> 00:07:38.466
Reports say China’s National Big Fund is leading the first-round financing of DeepSeek

00:07:38.466 --> 00:07:42.666
with a possible valuation of around US$45 billion

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:47.033
Other investors in talks reportedly include Tencent (00700),

00:07:47.033 --> 00:07:50.466
though the final lineup is not yet confirmed

00:07:50.466 --> 00:07:51.000
If true

00:07:51.000 --> 00:08:05.900
the Big Fund’s cross-sector investment in an AI model company marks a major strategic shift in China’s chip industry — moving from pure “hardware manufacturing” to deep “chip-model synergy

00:08:05.900 --> 00:08:06.333
”

00:08:06.333 --> 00:08:11.266
The far-reaching impact on the chip sector can be seen in four key dimensions:

00:08:11.666 --> 00:08:12.300
1

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:26.733
Accelerating “de-Nvidia-ization” of domestic chips — DeepSeek’s latest V4 series models explicitly support Huawei Ascend 950 super nodes 

00:08:26.733 --> 00:08:35.600
and have completed adaptation with eight domestic AI chip makers including Cambricon

00:08:35.766 --> 00:08:36.500
Hygon

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.300
and Moore Threads

00:08:38.733 --> 00:08:39.333
2

00:08:39.333 --> 00:08:44.033
Re-rating domestic computing chips — from “usable” to “high-performance”:

00:08:44.033 --> 00:08:48.133
The Big Fund’s participation injects market confidence

00:08:48.133 --> 00:08:55.933
proving domestic computing power can support trillion-parameter top-tier models

00:08:55.933 --> 00:08:58.700
Upstream players in semiconductor equipment

00:08:58.700 --> 00:08:59.900
advanced packaging

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:08.300
and memory will also benefit from rising localization rates (expected to reach 70% by 2030),

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:12.533
prompting the market to revalue domestic computing power

00:09:12.666 --> 00:09:13.266
3

00:09:13.266 --> 00:09:30.133
Building a “domestic chip + domestic model” commercial closed loop — DeepSeek-V4’s localization drastically lowers AI inference costs and helps form a complete “model-chip-cloud” ecosystem in China

00:09:30.133 --> 00:09:30.866
4

00:09:30.866 --> 00:09:36.100
Vertical integration of strategic resources — Previously focused on chip manufacturing (e

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:36.266
g

00:09:36.266 --> 00:09:36.833
SMIC),

00:09:36.833 --> 00:09:48.933
the Big Fund’s leadership in AI model financing shows the national strategy is now vertically integrating “computing supply” and “computing demand” 

00:09:48.933 --> 00:09:57.066
to ensure high-end AI model development is not disrupted by chip shortages under US export controls

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:57.966
Separately

00:09:57.966 --> 00:10:02.733
driven by strong AI chip demand and reports of cooperation with Apple

00:10:02.733 --> 00:10:05.966
Samsung shares soared on Wednesday

00:10:05.966 --> 00:10:09.300
hitting a record high of 270

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:15.666
000 KRW, up 16.13%,

00:10:15.833 --> 00:10:23.466
with market cap surpassing KRW 150 trillion (US$1.03 trillion).

00:10:23.733 --> 00:10:31.300
It becomes the second Asian company after TSMC to exceed US$1 trillion in market value

00:10:31.333 --> 00:10:40.866
Phillip Securities offers South Korean stock trading services with online commission at 0.35% (minimum KRW 20000 per trade

00:10:40.866 --> 00:10:41.066
approx

00:10:41.066 --> 00:10:42.400
HK$110–120).

00:10:42.866 --> 00:10:45.766
No custody fees for Korean stocks

00:10:45.800 --> 00:10:56.100
Well-known analyst Ming-Chi Kuo posted on X that OpenAI may be accelerating development of its first AI agent smartphone

00:10:56.100 --> 00:11:00.133
targeting mass production as early as the first half of next year

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:08.666
Reasons may include a favorable year-end listing window and intensifying competition in the AI agent phone segment

00:11:08.933 --> 00:11:17.300
MediaTek is currently the most likely to exclusively win the processor order

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:31.333
The device is expected to use a customized version based on the Dimensity 9600 and will be produced on TSMC’s enhanced 2nm process (N2P) in the second half

00:11:31.433 --> 00:11:34.000
If development goes smoothly

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:40.600
shipments are projected at around 30 million units combined for next year and the year after

00:11:41.033 --> 00:11:43.466
Hong Kong-listed property stocks mostly rose

00:11:43.466 --> 00:11:55.666
Recent positive news in the real estate sector has been frequent — from central government top-level guidance to local detailed rules — forming comprehensive policy support

00:11:55.733 --> 00:11:57.466
Following the central tone

00:11:57.466 --> 00:11:59.700
major cities including Guangzhou

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.700
Shenzhen, Tianjin, Suzhou

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:07.066
and Wuhan rolled out new property policies around the May 1 holiday

00:12:07.066 --> 00:12:10.100
creating a wave of policy momentum

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:12.766
During the May 1 holiday (May 1–5

00:12:12.766 --> 00:12:13.000
2026),

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:18.433
Shenzhen recorded 396 new and second-hand residential transactions citywide

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:21.933
New homes (pre-sale + ready) saw 275 registrations

00:12:21.933 --> 00:12:25.233
up 45.5% year-on-year;

00:12:25.233 --> 00:12:29.166
second-hand homes recorded 121 transactions

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:31.833
up 80.6% year-on-year

00:12:31.833 --> 00:12:37.600
The Nasdaq and S&amp;P 500 hit new record highs again on Wednesday

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:44.833
while oil prices fell after reports emerged that the US and Iran are close to reaching a peace agreement

00:12:44.833 --> 00:12:51.833
The “fear gauge” VIX index rose 0.01 point or 0.06% to 17.39

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:56.500
The Nasdaq surged 2% to 25,838;

00:12:56.500 --> 00:13:02.100
the S&amp;P 500 climbed 1.5% to 7365

00:13:02.233 --> 00:13:09.400
setting a new all-time closing high and posting its largest single-day gain since April 8

00:13:09.533 --> 00:13:14.666
The Dow Jones Industrial Average rose 1.2% to 49910

00:13:15.066 --> 00:13:17.666
The Nasdaq China Golden Dragon Index

00:13:17.666 --> 00:13:19.433
which tracks Chinese stocks

00:13:19.433 --> 00:13:26.100
jumped 237 points or 3.5% to close at 7127

00:13:26.266 --> 00:13:30.633
All sectors closed higher except Energy and Utilities

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:33.766
with Industrials and Technology leading the gains

00:13:33.766 --> 00:13:35.233
each up 2.6%.

00:13:35.233 --> 00:13:36.700
Advanced Micro Devices (AMD

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:39.433
US) shares skyrocketed nearly 19%,

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:43.533
making it one of the best performers in the S&amp;P 500

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:50.133
The chipmaker released better-than-expected first-quarter results after the market close on Tuesday

00:13:50.133 --> 00:13:57.800
driven by strong data centre revenue growth fueled by artificial intelligence infrastructure demand

00:13:57.833 --> 00:14:05.400
Analysts expect AMD to capture roughly half of the server CPU serviceable market

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:09.866
which is projected to exceed US$120 billion by 2030

00:14:09.866 --> 00:14:11.100
Nvidia (NVDA

00:14:11.100 --> 00:14:12.900
US) rose 5.8%.

00:14:13.133 --> 00:14:19.933
The company announced a multi-year collaboration with specialty glass manufacturer Corning (GLW

00:14:19.933 --> 00:14:29.200
US) to support AI factory construction and significantly expand optical fibre connectivity manufacturing capacity

00:14:29.433 --> 00:14:42.433
The partnership will increase Corning’s optical fibre connectivity manufacturing capacity in the US by 10 times and boost its domestic optical fibre production capacity by more than 50%.

00:14:43.233 --> 00:14:53.900
The expanded capacity will enable hyperscale data centres to deploy Nvidia accelerated computing at scale

00:14:54.133 --> 00:14:55.500
Corning shares rose 12%.

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:56.900
Walt Disney (DIS

00:14:56.900 --> 00:15:02.166
US) reported second-quarter results (ended March 28) that beat market expectations

00:15:02.166 --> 00:15:05.833
with revenue growth across all business segments

00:15:05.833 --> 00:15:12.200
The company also reaffirmed expectations for accelerated growth in the second half of the year

00:15:12.433 --> 00:15:16.666
Adjusted earnings per share came in at US$1.57

00:15:17.233 --> 00:15:24.900
higher than US$1.45 a year ago and above the consensus estimate of US$1.49

00:15:25.833 --> 00:15:31.233
Revenue rose 7% year-on-year to US$25.17 billion

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:35.600
beating expectations of US$24.87 billion

00:15:36.233 --> 00:15:48.100
Disney expects adjusted EPS for fiscal 2026 to grow 12% (excluding the 53rd week impact) or 16% including it

00:15:48.200 --> 00:15:51.733
compared to previous guidance of double-digit growth

00:15:51.733 --> 00:15:59.633
The company reiterated its forecast for double-digit adjusted EPS growth in fiscal 2027

00:15:59.900 --> 00:16:02.100
Its shares rose 7.5%,

00:16:02.933 --> 00:16:06.000
making it the best performer on the Dow

00:16:06.866 --> 00:16:08.500
Restaurant Brands International (QSR

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:08.666
US),

00:16:08.666 --> 00:16:10.533
the parent company of Burger King

00:16:10.533 --> 00:16:15.400
reported first-quarter earnings and revenue that exceeded market expectations

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:19.133
with comparable sales growth in line with forecasts

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:26.066
Adjusted EPS rose to US$0.86 from US$0.75 a year earlier;

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:30.700
revenue increased 7.4% to US$2.26 billion

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:37.466
beating estimates of US$0.83 and US$2.24 billion respectively

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:40.900
Comparable sales grew 3.2% year-on-year

00:16:40.900 --> 00:16:42.500
meeting expectations

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:45.233
Net restaurant count grew 2.6%,

00:16:45.466 --> 00:16:49.666
compared to 3.3% growth in the same period last year

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:57.633
The company maintained its outlook for comparable sales growth of over 3% from 2024 to 2028

00:16:57.633 --> 00:17:04.266
with net restaurant growth exceeding 5% by the end of the algorithmic period

00:17:04.266 --> 00:17:06.233
On the economic data front

00:17:06.333 --> 00:17:19.666
ADP reported that private payrolls increased by 109000 in April, up from 61000 in March — the fastest pace in over a year

00:17:19.666 --> 00:17:20.100
However

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:24.600
the figure fell short of market expectations of 120000

00:17:24.733 --> 00:17:33.433
indicating a stable labour market that is even showing signs of heating up despite the outbreak of the Iran conflict

00:17:33.966 --> 00:17:38.233
Our stock pick today is Prudential (2378)

00:17:38.266 --> 00:17:43.800
Prudential delivered another strong set of results in the first quarter of 2026

00:17:43.800 --> 00:17:47.900
with double-digit growth in new business profit once again

00:17:47.966 --> 00:17:52.133
The performance was broad-based across all business segments

00:17:52.133 --> 00:17:57.966
Both Annualised New Business Premiums (ANP) and new business profit margin rose

00:17:57.966 --> 00:18:00.366
confirming that the Group’s multi-channel

00:18:00.366 --> 00:18:02.533
multi-market business model

00:18:02.533 --> 00:18:09.433
together with disciplined execution and a continued focus on driving high-quality growth

00:18:09.433 --> 00:18:11.400
is working effectively

00:18:11.433 --> 00:18:14.433
The Group remains committed to value creation

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:20.833
continuously strengthening its distribution capabilities and enhancing customer experience

00:18:21.066 --> 00:18:26.766
It is well positioned to capture structural growth opportunities in Asia and Africa

00:18:26.766 --> 00:18:37.066
and is confident of achieving double-digit growth in key financial metrics for 2026 and meeting its 2027 financial targets

00:18:37.066 --> 00:18:38.100
In the first quarter

00:18:38.100 --> 00:18:39.866
all segments recorded growth

00:18:39.866 --> 00:18:41.800
with Hong Kong, Mainland China

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:45.400
and Malaysia delivering double-digit increases

00:18:45.533 --> 00:18:52.100
Annualized new business premiums rose 6% year-on-year to US$1.823 billion

00:18:52.866 --> 00:18:58.100
while new business profit increased 10% to US$686 million

00:18:58.766 --> 00:19:03.333
The new business profit margin expanded by 2 percentage points

00:19:03.333 --> 00:19:04.033
In Hong Kong

00:19:04.033 --> 00:19:11.800
both the agency and bancassurance channels reported growth in new business profit with margin expansion

00:19:11.833 --> 00:19:19.633
mainly driven by a higher proportion of health and protection products in ANP and pricing adjustments

00:19:19.633 --> 00:19:21.466
The Mainland China joint venture

00:19:21.466 --> 00:19:22.966
CITIC Prudential Life

00:19:23.133 --> 00:19:28.733
continued the strong ANP momentum seen in the second half of 2025

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:29.966
In Malaysia

00:19:29.966 --> 00:19:31.600
new business profit grew

00:19:31.600 --> 00:19:33.800
driven by the agency channel

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:37.200
Although bancassurance volume softened slightly

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:43.400
the profit margin still improved thanks to further optimisation of the product mix

00:19:43.566 --> 00:19:44.666
In Indonesia

00:19:44.666 --> 00:19:49.900
new business profit saw only modest growth due to a strong base last year

00:19:50.066 --> 00:19:53.433
but bancassurance recorded double-digit growth

00:19:53.433 --> 00:19:57.233
benefiting from deeper cooperation with BSI

00:19:57.400 --> 00:20:05.766
The Group will continue to focus on recruiting high-calibre talent for the agency channel to boost activity

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:06.833
In Singapore

00:20:06.833 --> 00:20:12.833
strong customer demand for savings and wealth products drove solid ANP growth

00:20:12.833 --> 00:20:17.100
with the agency channel performing particularly well

00:20:17.166 --> 00:20:31.033
The Group is taking targeted measures to expand its health and protection product portfolio in response to changes in co-payment requirements for certain health insurance plans announced earlier

00:20:31.233 --> 00:20:34.800
The “Growth Markets and Others” segment also delivered growth

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:36.733
mainly powered by Thailand

00:20:36.733 --> 00:20:41.166
supported by sustained strong demand for savings products

00:20:41.166 --> 00:20:46.033
as well as the associate ICICI Prudential Life in India

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:51.666
Although Taiwan’s overall growth moderated compared with previous strong periods

00:20:51.666 --> 00:20:55.966
progress in the broker channel remained satisfactory

00:20:55.966 --> 00:20:57.166
In asset management

00:20:57.166 --> 00:21:00.933
Eastspring recorded net fund inflows

00:21:00.933 --> 00:21:07.633
Assets under management stood at US$268.9 billion as of 31 March 2026 (31 December 2025:

00:21:07.633 --> 00:21:09.833
US$277.7 billion),

00:21:09.866 --> 00:21:14.600
supported by positive cash flows from the Group’s insurance business

00:21:14.666 --> 00:21:23.633
This reflects the scale benefits and synergies created by integrating life insurance and asset management capabilities

00:21:23.766 --> 00:21:26.166
Suggested buy price: HK$119

00:21:26.600 --> 00:21:28.500
Target price: HK$135

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:30.133
Stop-loss: HK$112

00:21:30.133 --> 00:21:33.533
(I do not hold the above stock)

